NonLinLoc location module

This module is intended to run after REAL association. By default the run
scripts read:

../REAL/*.phase_sel.txt
../Data/station.dat
../REAL/tt_db/mymodel.nd

and creates NonLinLoc inputs:

obs/station_coordinates.txt
obs/phases.obs
obs_files/Event_*.nlloc_obs
run/vel_model.nd
nlloc.in
loc2ssst.in

Typical use:

bash run_nonlinloc.sh

For iterative SSST relocation:

bash run_ssst_relocations.sh

The run scripts use binaries staged in the repository bin directory, or the
directory set with `NLL_BIN_DIR`:

../bin
NLL_BIN_DIR=/path/to/NonLinLoc/src/bin bash run_ssst_relocations.sh

If they are missing, build the needed programs from the repository root and
stage them with:

cmake -S src/NonLinLoc/src -B src/NonLinLoc/src/build
cmake --build src/NonLinLoc/src/build --target Vel2Grid Grid2Time NLLoc Loc2ssst LocSum -j
cd src
bash run_install.sh

Grid2Time is run once for P and once for S because GTFILES selects one phase
per run. The default grids use cubic 1 km cells because the Podvin-Lecomte
travel-time solver requires dx=dy=dz. The default -2 km grid top keeps the
current station elevations inside the model.

Before final locations, edit run_nonlinloc.sh for the study-specific grid,
reference point, datum shift, pick-error mode, and minimum phase count.
For SSST runs, edit run_ssst_relocations.sh for the same grid/datum settings
and the iteration count.

Pick uncertainty modes:

fixed: use the P and S errors set in the run script for every pick.
residual: use bounded REAL phase_sel residuals,
sigma = min(max(abs(residual), phase_floor), sigma_cap).
auto: use residuals when available and otherwise fall back to fixed errors.

The default floors are P=0.02 s and S=0.04 s. The default cap is 0.50 s.
